  "notes": "Ideal fully occupied CsCl-type B2 FeSi, identified in Fischer (2014), Sections 3.2 and 4.2/Figure 5; Pm-3m (No. 221), Fe 1a and Si 1b. Reference a is the measured Table S2 row 70 lattice at 42.7476826557 GPa and 1176.245 K. This compressed diffraction reference is separate from the extrapolated EOS V0. Only explicitly labelled Peritheos refits are executable. The published Fischer B2 coefficients remain in the source audit because their thermal normalization is unresolved.",
